FINANCIAL BUDGET ANALYSIS DASHBOARD
====================================

Author: Preya Shah
Project Type: Data Analysis / Financial Reporting
Tools: Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn, Plotly


PROJECT SUMMARY
---------------
This project analyzes financial budget performance by comparing 
budgeted amounts against actual spending and forecast data.

The solution automates financial reporting, identifies key variance drivers, 
and generates both static and interactive visual dashboards to support 
data-driven decision making.

The project demonstrates:
- Data cleaning and transformation
- Financial variance calculations
- Aggregation and group-based analysis
- Data visualization (static + interactive)
- Automated reporting output


BUSINESS PROBLEM
----------------
Organizations need clear visibility into how actual spending compares 
to planned budgets. Manual reporting is time-consuming and error-prone.

This project automates the process and highlights:
- Overspending categories
- Underspending trends
- Monthly financial performance
- Forecast alignment with actual spending


KEY FEATURES
------------

1. Financial Summary Report
   - Total Budget
   - Total Actual Spend
   - Total Variance (Amount and Percentage)
   - Reporting Period Range

2. Category-Level Variance Analysis
   - Aggregated budget and actual spend per category
   - Variance percentage ranking
   - Top 5 categories with highest deviation

3. Monthly Performance Tracking
   - Budget vs Actual comparison (bar chart)
   - Monthly variance trend line
   - Forecast comparison

4. Budget Distribution Analysis
   - Pie chart showing allocation by category

5. Interactive Dashboard
   - Plotly-based interactive visualization
   - Exported as: budget_trends.html


DATA PROCESSING STEPS
---------------------
- Imported CSV data using Pandas
- Converted date columns to datetime format
- Calculated variance and variance percentage
- Grouped data by Category and Period
- Generated summary metrics
- Created visualizations using Matplotlib and Plotly
- Exported processed report to CSV


INPUT REQUIREMENTS
------------------
File: PMSD-TestDatav2.csv

Required columns:
- Period (format: Jan-24, Feb-24, etc.)
- Category
- Budget
- Actual_Spend
- Forecast


HOW TO RUN
----------
1. Install dependencies:
   pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn plotly

2. Place PMSD-TestDatav2.csv in the project directory.

3. Run:
   python budget_analysis.py


OUTPUT FILES
------------
- budget_trends.html  (Interactive dashboard)
- budget_report.csv   (Processed financial dataset)


